{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,85p' artifacts/codexC/compare-vs-strata.md; tail -35 artifacts/codexC/llamacpp-moe-map.md; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"# llama.cpp versus Strata: components and proof obligations\n\nAssignment T-C, 2026-11-09. Offline static analysis of llama.cpp `31288c9c66e59377f7788d920678a565bb89dd37` and Strata `ffa80d73133ea5c548aefe57889a16e8085a938f`. No runtime or speed claims were measured. `L:` citations are relative to `/home/muk/projects/siminfeng/campaign/ref/llama.cpp`; `S:` citations are relative to `/home/muk/projects/Strata`. See [implementation map](llamacpp-moe-map.md) for expanded paths and [instrumentation options](instrumentation-options.md) for trace collection.\n\n**Conclusion:** llama.cpp already supplies router/top-k, indexed expert kernels, heterogeneous tensor scheduling, selective expert uploads, and an optional LRU GPU expert cache. To reproduce the requested Strata mechanism, the primary missing component is **per-routed-expert CPU/GPU partitioning with concurrent execution and correct combination**, plus residency policy/tooling and lifecycle controls. This is a source comparison of the named hit-hook/cache model; Strata also has newer verify-window, prefill and model-family paths. It is not a claim that every Strata invocation uses `session_loop` or the same cache policy.\n\n## Mechanism comparison\n\n| mechanism | llama.cpp | Strata | is the difference a missing component we'd have to build? | tool/test needed |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Granite MoE graph | Plain Granite MoE aliases Granite graph, uses normalized softmax top-k weights, SiLU gated experts, optional shared FFN. `L:src/models/models.h:1771-1778`; `L:src/models/granite.cpp:270-304`. | Hit-hook interface receives current router IDs and K, independent of a Granite implementation. `S:include/strata/core/hit_hook.hpp:28-39`. This comparison does not establish Granite compatibility in Strata. | **No** router invention needed if llama.cpp is the executor. **Yes** model-specific graph/kernel integration if creating a separate engine; do not assume Strata is a drop-in Granite oracle. | HF/GGUF conversion audit; fixed-input reference logits; dump router IDs/weights and per-layer residuals. |\n| Router selection and observability | Named logits, argsort/view top-k, selected weights and normalization; public eval callback. `L:src/llama-graph.cpp:2185-2313`; `L:include/llama.h:393-394`. | Current IDs are passed into Launch before CPU pool decisions; stale IDs are explicitly a documented correctness hazard. `S:include/strata/core/hit_hook.hpp:30-39`; actual calls at `S:src/core/session.cpp:729-732`. | **Yes**, an application trace collector and token/layer identity schema; graph computation already exists. | Complete K IDs/weights per input token and layer; changing-route fixture that detects previous-layer IDs. Do not infer complete traces from truncated tensor printing. |\n| Weight layout and expert addressing | GGUF stacks all E matrices per projection/layer; logical IDs select slices. `L:src/models/granite-moe.cpp:66-69`; `L:ggml/src/ggml.c:3413-3436`. | Cache stores expert blobs with uniform or sized slot offsets; source produces one expert blob. `S:include/strata/core/expert_cache.hpp:93-102,190-217`; `S:src/core/expert_source.cpp:5348-5359`. | **Yes**, a blob/slice adapter if implementing Strata-style combined expert slots; **no** need to reimplement GGUF parsing/indexed math for a llama.cpp baseline. | Tensor metadata inspector; quant block/stride-aware byte slicing; gate/up/down order checks and hash/readback verification. |\n| Static placement | `-ngl`, `--cpu-moe`, `--n-cpu-moe`, `-ot` place layers/tensors; regex cannot select one expert inside a stacked tensor. `L:common/arg.cpp:2757-2819`; `L:src/llama-model-loader.cpp:1233-1258`. | Residency is keyed by `(layer,expert)` and returns slot/-1, enabling a layer's selected set to span tiers. `S:include/strata/core/expert_cache.hpp:154-166`. | **No** for whole-layer/tensor placement. **Yes** per-expert dispatch if that is the desired behavior; placement flags alone cannot express it. | Assignment log at exact batch size; all-CPU/all-GPU/mixed-residency controls. |\n| Persistent GPU expert slots | **Present**, opt-in `--moe-cache-mib`; separate gate/up/down banks with layer views and extra padding slot. `L:src/llama-moe-cache.cpp:270-277,357-384`; `L:common/arg.cpp:2780-2789`. | `ExpertCache` owns VRAM storage and residency independently of compute, supports sized offsets. `S:include/strata/core/expert_cache.hpp:19-22,86-102`. | **No** fundamental slot-storage gap. Reuse/adapt llama.cpp cache or build equivalent storage only if another executor is chosen. Layout differs from Strata's combined blob slot. | Budget-to-slots accounting, guard padding, slot byte readback; stress mixed quant/layout groups and allocation failure. |\n| Residency map and consumer | Host I32 `[1,E]` maps per layer; GPU gather yields slot IDs consumed by indexed matmuls. `L:src/llama-moe-cache.cpp:379-381`; `L:src/llama-graph.cpp:2532-2571,1675-1679`. | Host residency vector plus device-facing dispatch fields; slot API returns `kNotResident`. `S:include/strata/core/expert_cache.hpp:154-166,266`; `S:include/strata/core/expert_source.hpp:563` and following token-graph fields. | **No** mapping concept gap. **Yes** a residency snapshot/version contract across CPU/GPU dispatch if introducing concurrent updates. | Assert logical expert -> slot -> matching bytes -> output; hold a stale-map update deliberately and ensure no consumer reads an unready slot. |\n| Admission and replacement | Group-wide **LRU**, mandatory insertion of selected misses when eligible; touched hits protected before evictions. `L:src/llama-moe-cache.cpp:72-118`. | Cache object's `admit` itself does not evict, with optional per-layer admission; external code can replace mappings. `S:include/strata/core/expert_cache.hpp:154-188`. Separate adaptive loop swaps same-layer experts by decayed use/gain. `S:src/program/generate.cpp:19839-19935`. | **Yes** policy abstraction/profile/adaptive policy if reproducing this behavior. Do not describe Strata as having no eviction globally merely because `admit` does not evict. | Offline LRU versus static frequency versus decayed-use simulation; held-out prompts; churn, unique-expert hits and byte-weighted cost curves; tiny-cache adversarial trace. |\n| Profile-filled startup | Inspected cache initializes maps to -1 and fills on demand; no ranked-profile loader in this cache. `L:src/llama-moe-cache.cpp:418-424,548-577`. | Ranked `STRP` profiles, startup fill and verification; adaptive learned-profile save API. `S:include/strata/core/expert_cache.hpp:40-73`; `S:src/program/generate.cpp:5572,8050-8069`. | **Yes** trace-to-profile compiler, validation, preload and held-out evaluator. | `S:tools/make_profile.py:1-25,44-69` supplies format inspiration, but hard-codes 48 layers: make our tool metadata-driven for Granite. Ensure `--reorder`/no-base semantics actually use traces. |\n| Miss execution | Cache path synchronizes/readbacks IDs, uploads misses into slots, then computes all selected experts on GPU. Bypass path may execute CPU or selectively upload depending on scheduler. `L:src/llama-moe-cache.cpp:548-580`; `L:src/llama-context.cpp:2772-2843`. | Hit hook asks residency, may admit/fill a free slot, otherwise leaves a miss for CPU. CPU job pool skips/zeroes GPU-owned rows. `S:src/core/expert_source.cpp:5331-5369,4798-4828`. | **Yes, central gap:** same-layer routed expert partition, CPU miss worker pool integration and GPU hit list generation. Existing CPU kernels can be reused but scheduler has no equivalent HitFn seam. | Force none/all/some of K resident; compare every expert output and weighted sum to reference. Count each selected expert exactly once. |\n| GPU hits / CPU misses overlap | Scheduler splits and async c